CHAPTER VI

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 23

1. The City Regional Government has the obligation to strengthen community participation in the implementation of women's protection.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in the form of:a. prevention;
b. services and referrals;
c. development of data information systems;
d. strengthening of service institutions;
e. research and policy advocacy;
f. control, guidance and supervision;and g. financing.
3. Strengthening community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), can be carried out by:a. strengthening cooperation;andb. strengthening institutional capacity for prevention and services from the community, boarding educational institutions, and business world.
4. The business world has responsibility in the implementation of Women's Protection in accordance with the targets of Corporate Social and Environmental Responsibility.

14 - (5) The form of business world responsibility as referred to in paragraph (4), is carried out as follows: a. financial assistance to service institutions; b. empowerment;
c. capacity building;
d. publication and information media;
e. provision of infrastructure;
f. establishment of special institutions for prevention and violence complaint services;andg. non-binding social assistance.

