CHAPTER II

WOMEN'S RIGHTS

Article 5

Every Woman has the right to:
a. obtain information related to the Protection of Women, victim service procedures and developments in case handling;
b. report, provide statements and views without pressure;
c. participate in case handling and in efforts - 7 - to eliminate violence against women;
d. obtain protection of confidentiality; e. obtain protection for the security of self, family and property from threats and violence;
f. be free from all forms of stereotypes, stigma and other discrimination;
g. obtain services and recovery needed; h. obtain restitution; and i. form and join organizations.

Article 3

Women's Protection aims to:
a. prevent all forms of violence, exploitation, and discrimination against women;
b. provide services and recovery for women victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination; c. realize the capacity of the City Regional Government in the implementation of Women's Protection from violence, exploitation and discrimination;
d. increase community participation in Women's Protection; ande. realize a social life that is safe and free from all forms of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women.

Article 8

1. The prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is carried out in the following sectors: a. education;
b. health;
c. religion;
d. security;
e. justice;
f. public works and spatial planning;
g. public housing and residential areas; h. social affairs;

8 -
i. labor;
j. women's empowerment and child protection; k. defense;
l. environment;
m. population administration and civil registration; n. population control and family planning; o. transportation;
p. communication and informatics;
q. cooperatives, small and medium enterprises;
r. youth and sports;
s. culture;
t. tourism;
u. trade and industry; and v. other sectors.
2. The prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out by: a. developing communication media, information, education and public campaigns through media;
b. developing educational materials and curriculum according to regional authority;
c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. building early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential environments, educational environments, boarding educational environments, and other public spaces;
e. implementing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic boarding school students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
f. encouraging behavioral change of parents and society;
g. developing regional policies, schools, boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
h. forming and developing cadres, communities, young people, students, Islamic boarding school students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, community leaders and religious leaders for prevention;
i. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
j. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
k. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
l. increasing the capacity of the City Regional Government, government agencies, educational institutions, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities;
m. conducting cooperation with religious institutions, community social institutions, service institutions, - 9 - universities, media, youth organizations, religious leaders and community leaders; and n. conducting socialization of laws and regulations. (3) The sectors and forms of prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are implemented by agencies, regional apparatus, institutions, community institutions, organizations, communities, professional institutions that handle related affairs according to their authority based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

